         ],
         "text": [
            {
                "text": "#### Objects\n\nIn this region, several museums hold metates like the one in the photo. They are stones used to grind corn.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<img src=\"http://www.historytracers.org/images/SanJoseCRMuseo/SanJoseCRAntropologia.jpg\" id=\"img0\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img0', '0%')\"  class=\"imgcenter\"/>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": [],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "*Photo taken in <htdate0></span>, during a visit to the Museum of Anthropology, San José, Costa Rica*",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2015",
                     "month": "10",
                     "day": "17"
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "ba0cae93-4516-4f24-a616-0c0d79372569",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "ba0cae93-4516-4f24-a616-0c0d79372569",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "thinking",
         "source_menu": [],
         "text": [
            {
                "text": "How can we tell if these objects were made by a single people and taken to other regions? Or were they created separately by different peoples?",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "51c8e018-dd46-4bae-9a51-7af416dc31e0",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": "yes",
         "score": 2,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "51c8e018-dd46-4bae-9a51-7af416dc31e0",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "shocking",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "3fb52297-2d42-46f2-8ef1-b8a2c8f4052a",
               "text": "HOOPES, J. W, pp. 459",
               "page": "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/225268005_Sorcery_and_the_Taking_of_Trophy_Heads_in_Ancient_Costa_Rica",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            },
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "ffffd208-eb09-4da3-b516-f8bc695758dd",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=ffffd208-eb09-4da3-b516-f8bc695758dd",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
                "text": "#### Beyond Appearances\n\nJust comparing height and width is not enough. We also need to check the age of the object — or of other objects found in the same place.\n\nFor the metates, other evidence shows they were made in Costa Rica, where most examples are found.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "1304d59e-9777-418e-a4d6-ddd3d57e34d5",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "1304d59e-9777-418e-a4d6-ddd3d57e34d5",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "party",
         "source_menu": [],
         "text": [
            {
                "text": "#### Conclusion\n\nTo tell if two things are equal, looking at appearance alone is not enough. You need to look at the context — what is around them.\n\nWe saw this in practice with a Mesoamerican metate.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
